[Applause]  the moment australia's new prime  minister acknowledges his victory  leading the labour party to power for  the first time since 2010. i'm honored  to be given the opportunity to serve as  the 31st prime minister of australia  an mp for 25 years anthony albanese is  one of australia's longest serving  politicians who came from a humble  background and campaigned on a platform  of unity and optimism  it says a lot about our great country  that the son of a single mom who is a  disability pensioner  who grew up in public housing down the  road in camperdown  can stand before you tonight as  australia's prime minister  i have put forward  a positive clear plan for a better  future for our country  and i have shared the two principles  that will drive a government that i lead  no one left behind  because we should always look after the  disadvantaged and the vulnerable  but also no one held back  a phone call from incumbent scott  morrison to the labour leader conceded  his party had lost power after nine  years  thank you so much for standing  by us at this time and i know you will  continue to do that into the future to  my colleagues tonight  who have had to deal with very difficult  news and have lost their seats tonight i  as leader take responsibility for the  wins and the losses that is the burden  and that is the responsibility of  leadership and as a result i will be  handing over the leadership at the next  party room meeting  just who will replace morrison's liberal  leader remains to be seen his deputy and  treasurer of the country josh feidenberg  lost his seat to an independent  it was always going to be a tight race  outgoing prime minister scott morrison  marginally behind in the polls in the  lead up to the election  unlike in 2019 the polls run true this  time round  climate change was the driving election  issue the morrison government was not  thought to be doing enough in the global  fight as bushfires and floods devastated  australia's 